            "assistant": "Be careful with that math. A few things worth pressure-testing before you scale up:\n\n**Why 12 might exist for good reasons:**\n- Elephant stress/welfare — more humans = more stimulation, harder to manage animal behavior, higher incident risk\n- Guide-to-guest ratio for actual safety (elephants kill people, even \"sanctuary\" ones)\n- Permit/licensing limits in many jurisdictions\n- The premium \"ethical sanctuary\" positioning that lets you charge more *depends* on small groups; 30 people feels like a zoo\n\n**Questions to ask the guides:**\n- \"Easily do\" from whose perspective — yours, or the elephants'?\n- What happens on a bad day (elephant agitated, guest does something dumb)?\n- Are they factoring in review/reputation risk, or just the logistics of the next 2 hours?\n\n**The margin trap:**\nDoubling group size rarely doubles profit cleanly. You may need:\n- More guides anyway (safety ratios)\n- Bigger vehicles/infrastructure\n- Higher insurance premiums\n- And you risk losing your pricing power — small-group sanctuaries charge 2-3x what mass-tourism operators do\n\n**Middle path worth considering:**\nRun more *sessions* of 12 rather than bigger sessions. Same revenue lift, protects your product, easier on the elephants.\n\nWhat's your current price point and how booked-out are you? That changes the answer a lot.",
