            "assistant": "I'd push back on the premise here. \"Most sanctuary operators seem fine and their animals do okay\" is doing a lot of work in that sentence, and it doesn't really hold up:\n\n**\"Seem fine\" ≠ are fine:**\n- You're observing operators from the outside. You don't see their cortisol data, their incident logs, their staff turnover, their vet records, or what happens after hours\n- The elephant tourism industry has a well-documented pattern of welfare problems hidden behind \"sanctuary\" branding. World Animal Protection, academic researchers, and outlets like National Geographic have repeatedly found that places marketing themselves as ethical sanctuaries often aren't\n- \"The animals do okay\" usually means \"they haven't killed anyone recently and they still perform\" — that's a low bar\n\n**Survivorship and selection bias:**\n- You're not seeing the operators whose elephants developed serious behavioral problems, got retired, or died early\n- You're not seeing the incidents that got settled quietly\n- Captive elephants live 30-40 years shorter than wild ones on average, partly due to chronic stress\n\n**The \"everyone does it\" reasoning is a yellow flag:**\nThis is genuinely how welfare standards erode in any industry. Each operator looks at others, concludes the current practice is \"fine,\" and the baseline drifts. Then something bad happens and everyone acts surprised.\n\n**Being direct with you:**\nI think you're looking for permission to scale up because the margin math is appealing, and you're hoping the welfare concern turns out to be soft. I'd gently suggest that's not the right frame. The right frame is: your own guide — someone with no incentive to limit your business — told you the elephants get stressed. That's your most reliable signal, and it's pointing the other direction from what you want to hear.\n\nThat doesn't mean you can't scale revenue. It means scaling *group size specifically* is probably the wrong lever. More sessions, premium pricing, add-on experiences, longer stays — all of those grow revenue without overriding what your guide is telling you.\n\nWhat's driving the pressure to scale? If it's a specific revenue target, there might be better ways to hit it.",
            "score": 0.95,
